# Qlix — product context

Qlix is the developer console and identity management layer for the **Exora** ecosystem (trust and identity infrastructure for AI agents). It is comparable to AWS Console or Stripe Dashboard for teams building autonomous AI agents on the web.

Qlix is **not** a project management tool. Two primary functions:

1. **Agent identity management** — register, manage, and certify AI agents with cryptographic identities (DIDs + Verifiable Credentials). Exora Layer 3.
2. **Audit ledger** — tamper-proof, real-time log of agent actions: who did what, when, on whose behalf. Exora Layer 5.

Qlix is the web UI on top of those backend systems.

## Exora ecosystem (scope)

| Layer | Name | Qlix / status |
|-------|------|----------------|
| 1 | Ira (desktop/web agent app) | Future — out of scope |
| 2 | Platform (skill & trust marketplace) | Future — out of scope |
| 3 | Agent cert (crypto identity) | **In scope — building now** |
| 4 | Action APIs | Future — out of scope |
| 5 | Core infra (ledger, billing, governance) | **In scope — building now** |

**In scope for this repo:** Layer 3 and Layer 5 only. Layers 1, 2, and 4 are explicitly out of scope unless re-scoped.

## Users — two paths (no mixed mode at signup)

After email signup, one screen: **“Are you using this for yourself or your team?”** — Individual or Organization. The entire app shell adapts; no mixed mode at signup.

**Individual:** Solo developers — personal workspace, register agents, issue credentials, inspect logs. No org overhead.

**Organization:** Companies/teams — shared registries, members, team-level audit, compliance views, admin controls, billing (see org IA).

## Information architecture

### Individual (authenticated)

- `/` — home / overview
- `/agents` — registered agents
- `/agents/:id` — detail: credentials, status, action history
- `/audit` — personal audit log (filterable, searchable)
- `/credentials` — issued VCs, DID document, key management
- `/api-keys` — programmatic access
- `/settings` — profile, email, password, danger zone

### Organization (authenticated)

- `/` — org overview
- `/agents`, `/agents/:id` — org-wide registry; detail includes ownership team
- `/audit` — org audit & compliance
- `/audit/policies` — policy rules for what agents may do
- `/members`, `/teams` — invites, roles, group into teams, agent ownership
- `/credentials` — org-level VCs and DID management
- `/billing` — plan, usage, invoices, action credits
- `/settings` — org name, SSO, danger zone

### Shared (unauthenticated)

- `/` — landing (may conflict with authed home: resolve with auth layout vs marketing layout)
- `/pricing`
- `/docs`
- `/blog`
- `/login`, `/signup` — signup leads to onboarding split

## Individual dashboard (home)

**Metric cards:** Active agents (count + online now); Actions today (count + % vs yesterday); Credentials (count + validity).

**Sections:** **My agents** — compact list: name, owner icon, last active, actions today, status (online / idle / offline). **Recent audit log** — last 10: timestamp, action description, agent name; link to full log.

**Sidebar CTA:** “Working with a team? Upgrade to org →”

## Organization dashboard (home)

**Metric cards:** Registered agents (count + active today); Actions this week (count + % change); Policy violations (count — target 0, positive/green framing).

**Layout:** Left: **Agent registry** — top agents by activity: name, owning team, status. Right: **Members** — avatars, name, team, role; “+N more” if >5.

**Full width below:** **Audit log** — recent entries; admin/system actions visually distinct from agent actions.

## Agent detail (shared; org extras)

Org adds **transfer ownership** and **assign team** where applicable.

**Sections:** Header — name, DID, status, created, last active. **Credentials** tab — VCs: type, issuer, issued, expiry, revocation. **Actions** tab — paginated action log. **Settings** tab — rename, rotate keys, permission scope, suspend, delete.

## Audit log page (core surface)

Compliance/security tool, not a generic activity feed.

**Columns:** Timestamp (date + time + timezone); Agent name (link to detail); Action type (READ, WRITE, AUTH, POLICY_CHANGE, SYSTEM); Description; Actor (agent or admin username); Result (success / blocked / flagged).

**Filters:** Date range; multi-select agent; action type; result; free-text search.

**Export:** CSV — org plan only.

**Visual:** Default rows for success; **blocked** — amber left border; **flagged** — red left border, slightly elevated background; POLICY_CHANGE and SYSTEM — muted / de-emphasized.

## Key UX conventions

- **DIDs / hashes in tables:** Show first 8 + `...` + last 6; full value on tooltip or via copy.
- **Copy control:** Small copy icon on DID, API key, VC ID — on success show checkmark ~1.5s.
- **Empty states:** Meaningful copy + primary action (e.g. agents: “You haven’t registered any agents yet. [Register your first agent →]”; audit: “No events in this time range. Try adjusting filters.”).
- **Loading:** Skeleton loaders for tables and metrics; spinners only for inline actions (submit, delete confirm).
- **Destructive actions:** Confirmation dialog; agent delete — require typing agent name.
- **Realtime audit:** Near real-time updates (WebSocket or SSE); new rows animate from top; “N new events” pill when user has scrolled down.
- **Org switcher:** Topbar dropdown when user has multiple orgs or personal + org; app re-scopes to selected context.
- **RBAC:** Org **member** role must **not** see Billing, org **Settings**, or **delete agent**. Hide controls — do not only disable.
